-- title:
--   Glued addition morphism computes `addMap` when Δ≠ 0
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $R$, and $F$ a field that is an $R$-algebra in which the image of the discriminant $W.\Delta$ under $\operatorname{algebraMap} R F$ is non-zero. Assume the three gluing hypotheses for $W$: `KwLRSixUCoverage`, that for all $i,j\in\{0,1,2\}$ the range of `kw_lrSixU W i j` generates the unit ideal of $\mathcal A_i\otimes_R\mathcal A_j$; `KwLRPerChartCompat`, that for all $i,j$ and all $l,l'\in \mathrm{Fin}\,3\oplus\mathrm{Fin}\,3$ the two morphisms `kw_lrSixU_toE` agree after the two projections of the pullback of the localisation maps `kw_lrSixU_locMap`; and `KwLROuterCompat`, the analogous agreement of the morphisms `kw_lrOuter_toE` over the cover `kwProjPullbackOpenCoverCR` indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,3\times\mathrm{Fin}\,3$, so that these glue to `kw_lrAddMorphism` on the pullback of `projModelStrCR W.toProjective` with itself. Here the grading is the one induced on $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\,3,R)$ modulo the homogeneous ideal generated by the projective Weierstrass polynomial of $W$. Given indices $i,j,k$, $R$-algebra maps $\psi_i,\psi_j,\psi_k$ from the degree-zero homogeneous localisations away from the classes of $X_i,X_j,X_k$ to $F$, and two $F$-points $x,y$ of the Proj model over $\operatorname{Spec} F\to\operatorname{Spec} R$ (morphisms to `Proj` whose composite with `projModelStrCR W.toProjective` is `Spec.map (algebraMap R F)`) such that $x.1$ is $\operatorname{Spec}\psi_i$ followed by the $i$-th map of `projModelAffineOpenCoverCR` and $y.1$ is $\operatorname{Spec}\psi_j$ followed by its $j$-th map, suppose the pullback lift of $x.1,y.1$ followed by `kw_lrAddMorphism W hcov hcompat houter` equals $\operatorname{Spec}\psi_k$ followed by the $k$-th map of the cover. Then, in `WeierstrassCurve.Projective.PointClass F`, the class of the triple $(\psi_k(\mathrm{gen}\,k\,0),\psi_k(\mathrm{gen}\,k\,1),\psi_k(\mathrm{gen}\,k\,2))$ equals the value of `addMap` for the base-changed projective curve $(W.\mathrm{baseChange}\,F).\mathrm{toProjective}$ on the classes of the corresponding triples for $\psi_i$ and $\psi_j$.
--
--   This is the compatibility statement identifying the scheme-theoretic addition morphism on the projective Weierstrass model with the formula-based addition of projective point classes, for $F$-valued points given in charts, under non-vanishing of the discriminant in $F$. It is used to transport the group-law identities for the glued morphism, being cited by the associativity, commutativity and identity-section statements `addMorphism_assoc`, `addMorphism_comm` and `addMorphism_mul_zeroSect`.
